[00:14.47] Once I walked through the halls of a station
[00:21.72] Someone called your name
[00:28.92] In the street I heard children laughing
[00:35.37] They all sound the same
[00:42.56] Wonder, could you ever know me
[00:49.94] Know the reason why I live
[00:57.26] Is there nothing you can show me
[01:03.01] Life seems so little to give
[01:10.76] Once I climbed up the face of a mountain
[01:17.58] And ate the wild fruit there
[01:24.76] Fell asleep until the moonlight woke me
[01:31.15] And I could taste your hair
[01:38.33] Isn't everybody dreaming!
[01:46.04] Then the voice I hear is real
[01:52.30] Out of all the idle scheming
[01:58.28] Can't we have something to feel
[02:19.94] Once upon a time leaves me empty
[02:26.79] Tomorrow never comes
[02:34.63] I could sing the sound of your laughter
[02:40.58] Still I don't know your name
[02:47.71] Must be some way to repay you
[02:55.06] Out of all the good you gave
[03:01.85] If a rumor should delay you
[03:08.16] Love seems so little to save
[03:23.02] 